			"name": "executionContexts",
			"description": "Execution contexts (an experiment: turn it on with experimentSet or at /account/experiments): run code on your own laptop, home server, or build box running `kody daemon` instead of Kody cloud, with the folders and LAN access you allow. `kody connect` registers a machine and installs the daemon as a background service (`kody daemon install`: systemd on Linux, launchd on macOS, a per-user Task Scheduler logon task on Windows) so it survives reboots. Windows runs use native host paths like C:\\Users\\you\\project. Also sharing and your per-org fallback chain. Guide: guide:execution_contexts.",
